  "content": {
    "title": "ABC pulls upcoming season of 'The Bachelorette,' which featured a Carmel man",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 6:31 p.m. ETA Carmel resident was set to compete for roses and the ring on the upcoming season of \"The Bachelorette,\" but the show will no longer make it to air.ABC announced that it's pulling season 22 of \"The Bachelorette\" because its lead, \"Secret Lives of Mormon Wives\" star Taylor Frankie Paul, faces an ongoing domestic violence investigation. Matt Carroll, a 43-year-old Carmel resident and former Purdue basketball forward, was cast as one of the 22 men pursuing Paul. The premiere was set for March 22.ABC has not announced whether additional filming will take place with the original cast of men or whether the filmed season will air at a later date. Neither Carroll nor representatives for \"The Bachelorette\" immediately responded to requests for comment.Why was Taylor Frankie Paul's season of 'The Bachelorette' canceled?The cancellation comes amid a recently released video from a 2023 incident involving Paul and her ex, Dakota Mortensen. On March 19 TMZ released footage in which Paul seemingly attacks Mortensen and throws chairs at him. The 2024 pilot of \"Secret Lives of Mormon Wives\" depicted police showing up at the scene but did not share the details of what had happened beforehand. After the incident, Paul pleaded guilty to one count of aggravated assault. She also faced charges of child abuse, criminal mischief and domestic violence in the presence of a child but those were dismissed. “In light of the newly released video just surfaced today, we have made the decision to not move forward with the new season of ‘The Bachelorette’ at this time,\" Disney Entertainment Television said in a statement to USA Today. \"Our focus is on supporting the family.”Paul and Mortensen have since been embroiled in a tumultuous on-again, off-again relationship that makes for much of the plot on \"Secret Lives,\" including the show's fourth season that premiered March 12 on Hulu.Speculation about an additional domestic violence incident surfaced earlier this week, with claims that Mortensen's roommate called the police after an explosive argument between him and Paul Feb. 24 or 25. Filming for the fifth season of \"The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives\" has since paused, and Cinnabon has backed out as a sponsor on both shows.Utah's Draper City Police Department confirmed it was investigating an incident but declined to comment further, according to NBC News.Who is Matt Carroll? Meet the former Purdue basketball forward who was set for this season of 'The Bachelorette'Carroll is an industrial real estate broker and divorced father of three. At 43, the Carmel resident was the oldest of the bunch, and he was ready to “build a future with someone who makes him truly feel chosen,” according to his official bio on “The Bachelorette” website.Carroll grew up in Guatemala and the United Kingdom before enrolling at Purdue. Standing 6'8,\" he was a forward for the Boilermakers from 2001 to 2006, redshirting his sophomore year. He's now an industrial real estate broker based in Carmel and co-host of the \"Circle City Success\" podcast, for which he interviews different business figures around the Indianapolis area.Contact IndyStar Pop Culture Reporter Heather Bushman at hbushman@indystar.com",
